The acyclic tracker. Every command prints one JSON document

Usage: acyclic [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init      Sets up a tracker clone as a new replica, creating the repository if there is none
  prime     Prints conventions for agents, matched to this version, as text
  ready     Lists ready leaves, best first
  show      Shows an item with its role, readiness and claims
  claim     Claims a ready leaf, or renews the actor's claim
  done      Marks an item done, with evidence
  needs     Lists what needs the user
  level     Sets the autonomy level, globally or for a thread (the user's)
  import    Imports a plan: adds and updates what the document names, and never deletes
  doctor    Lists entities that can't be read
  item      Adds, edits, moves, reopens or archives items, or sets their state
  link      Adds or removes links between items
  thread    Creates or edits threads, and puts items in them; agents' edits to approved threads wait as proposals
  repo      Creates or edits repository records, and attaches them to items or threads
  proposal  Keeps or drops proposals (the user's)

Options:
      --tracker <TRACKER>  The tracker clone; otherwise `ACYCLIC_TRACKER`, else the mapping in ~/.config/acyclic/trackers.toml
      --actor <ACTOR>      Who acts; otherwise `ACYCLIC_ACTOR`, else `agent/undeclared`. The user must say so on the command
      --as-user            Act as the user
  -h, --help               Print help
  -V, --version            Print version
